('A7','Apply the GENERAL proper morphism theorem Stacks37.50.3, Tag0D2S, to f:X1->S1, the actual invertible M1=M_g modulo a, and the sole point s. Its hypotheses are proper morphism, invertible sheaf, and ample restriction on the fibre. No Noetherian base, flatness or finite-presentation strengthening is required by the statement. It gives an open neighborhood W of s on which M1 is relatively ample. Because S1 has ONE point, W=S1. Thus M1 is relatively ample on the ENTIRE actual modulo-a scheme. Since S1 is affine, M1 is also ample as an invertible sheaf on X1.'),
